-- Generated by gen_travelnet.ps1 from the
-- client's TaxiNodes, TaxiPath, TaxiPathNode, TransportAnimation, AreaTrigger,
-- Map, UiMap, UiMapAssignment (wago.tools, build 1.60.1.70450),
-- and from vmangos' world database (github.com/vmangos/core, GPL-2.0-or-later;
-- taxi_path_transitions, gameobject, gameobject_template, transports). Do not edit.
-- The travel network for route planning: 66 flight masters, 288 flight paths, 12
-- boats, zeppelins and ferries with 25 stops, the Deeprun Tram. Maps (continent IDs) used: 0 Eastern Kingdoms, 1 Kalimdor, 2991 Zephras Isle.
-- Coordinates are world yards as in the DB2 tables (TaxiNodes.Pos_0/Pos_1,
-- TaxiPathNode.Loc_0/Loc_1): x first, then y, the same frame as
-- C_Map.GetWorldPosFromMapPos(...).x/.y (Stormwind's flight master is x -8833, y 479).
-- Flight paths: the TaxiPath rows between two different flight masters that
-- are no transport, lie on open-world maps (Map.InstanceType 0; drops Alterac
-- Valley) and whose ends are not retired or helper nodes (names zzOLD...,
-- Quest Path ..., Transport, ..., Generic, ...). A free row counts only if the
-- reverse row exists too (keeps Auberdine - Rut'theran; drops one-way free
-- flights: Nighthaven druid flights, Eastern Plaguelands towers, the old
-- Southshore ferry). A second row with the same ends is left out. Length =
-- sum of the 3D distances between the path's waypoints in NodeIndex order.
-- Flight masters: the nodes these paths use (a node no kept path uses is left out).
-- Transports: the TaxiPath rows with docking waypoints (TaxiPathNode flag 2;
-- its Delay = seconds docked). The waypoints loop. A stop is where it docks,
-- on the waypoint's ContinentID; two docking points 10 yd or less apart in a row are
-- one stop (waits added). Legs leave out jumps: a change of map, the step after
-- a waypoint with flag 1 (teleport), and the step from the last waypoint back
-- to the first when it is longer than every other step of the path. A
-- transport docking only once is left out (path 436, Naxxramas). A transport
-- whose every stop is a dock of a newer one (higher path ID) is left out: path 295 (its docks are path 11167's);
-- WoW Forever sails path 11167 via Southshore from the same docks, no ship of
-- path 295 was seen in Forever (the audit of 2026-10-08).
-- Ride times: the server's path model (TrinityCore's TransportMgr::GeneratePath,
-- as the 1.12 servers move transports) on these waypoints: 30 yd/s, speeding up and
-- braking at 1 yd/s^2 around each stop (moveSpeed and accelRate of every
-- boat and zeppelin in Forever's gameobject cache of build 70245). Checked against
-- vmangos' measured rounds (transports.period):
--   241 350.7/350.8 s, 302 356.2/356.3 s, 285 303.3/303.5 s, 292 329.2/329.3 s,
--   293 316.0/316.3 s, 295 295.5/295.6 s, 301 332.9/333.0 s, 303 316.9/317.0 s
-- (path model/vmangos). The wait for a boat is half its round (you come at any time).
-- Multi-hop flights: vmangos' taxi_path_transitions on Forever's waypoints (355 of
-- 355 rows; the rest: a path not here or other towns). Checked against Leatrix
-- Plus' measured Forever flights (only checked, nothing taken; 2026-10-08): 319 two-hop
-- routes with a row, row minus measured: median +0.2 s; the hub's median for
-- the 150 without a row of their own: |difference| median 1.2 s, 90 % within 6.1 s.
-- Names: each stop after the nearest flight master within 600 yd on its map (the
-- town before the comma), else its zone map (UiMapAssignment), else its map.

